I remember the warning: this is not a game anymore. I can retreat to town if I need to, but the road forward will not open itself. A few players are visible in the distance; none close enough to save me from a bad decision.

The ${enemy.toLowerCase()} has noticed me. It lowers its shoulders, preparing to strike.`,choices:['Engage carefully. Watch for an opening.','Keep distance and study its movement before committing.','Retreat to the safe zone. I’m not ready for a fight.']};}
 if(s.storyKey==='ending')return {title:'THE CASTLE FALLS',label:'AINCRAD · FLOOR 100',text:`I stand beneath the final sky. The long climb across one hundred floors—every retreat, every party, every loss—has led here. Kirito and Asuna remain at the heart of the fight, and the survivors who made it this far stand together. My choices did not replace theirs. They helped make a path wide enough for all of us.

The last gate opens. The system’s red light fades. Somewhere beyond this world, ten thousand people are about to wake. I look back once at the castle that tried to become our whole world, then step toward the light.`,choices:['Begin the final encounter.']};
 if(s.storyKey==='afterBattle')return {title:'FIRST BLOOD',label:'FLOOR 1 · OUTER FIELD',text:`The Grey Wolf dissolves into blue polygons. For a moment I can hear only my own breathing. My hands are shaking—not because the fight was grand, but because it was real.

A system message confirms the kill. The first step has been taken, and the path back to the city is still open. Beyond the rise, I catch a glimpse of a party moving in formation. Their leader’s red hair flashes in the sun. Maybe it was the same player from the plaza.

What matters now is whether I keep going, and who I choose to become along the way.`,choices:['Return to the Starting City to recover and resupply.','Follow the party at a respectful distance.','Explore the nearby ruins; there may be a hidden cache.']};
 if(s.storyKey==='town')return townScene();
 if(s.storyKey==='questDone')return {title:'A SMALL VICTORY',label:`FLOOR ${s.floor} · ${esc(s.location.toUpperCase())}`,text:`A little experience, a few Col, and the memory of a difficult first fight. None of it makes me invincible. It does make the next step feel possible. The city is loud with rumors: a beta tester called Kirito has been marked a “beater” by the crowd, a new frontline group is forming, and the first boss is still somewhere at the top of a labyrinth.

For now, the adventure is local. I can train, prepare, or head back into the field.`,choices:['Check the town market and equipment stalls.','Rest at the inn, then return to the field.','Ask around for a side quest.','Head back out and search for another monster.']};

